## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates a practical lock-free pattern for data reads that must remain consistent without heavy synchronization.

## Key Concepts
- sequence lock
- memory_order_acquire/release
- barrier considerations on x86 vs ARM

## Code Example
```c
typedef struct { uint64_t ver; Config cfg128; } SharedConfig;

void write_config(SharedConfig* sc, Config new_cfg) {
  __atomic_fetch_add(&sc->ver, 1, memory_order_acq_rel); // make odd
  sc->cfg128 = new_cfg;
  __atomic_fetch_add(&sc->ver, 1, memory_order_release); // make even
}

Config read_config(SharedConfig* sc) {
  Config c;
  uint64_t v;
  do {
    v = __atomic_load_n(&sc->ver, memory_order_acquire);
    if (v & 1) continue;
    c = sc->cfg128;
  } while (__atomic_load_n(&sc->ver, memory_order_acquire) != v);
  return c;
}
```

